arcade-catalog.json contains dependency metadata exported from:
https://github.com/blueminder/flycast-dojo/blob/d0e47e572b1e7b355e88bda8308c89d0c5156cbf/core/hw/naomi/naomi_roms.cpp

Flycast native table: Copyright 2021 flyinghead, GPL-2.0-or-later.
ROM information from MAME (https://github.com/mamedev/mame), LGPL-2.1-or-later.
Copyright holders: Samuele Zannoli, R. Belmont, ElSemi, David Haywood,
Angelo Salese, Olivier Galibert, MetalliC.

Generated by TrainerOS generate-arcade-catalog.py. Exported fields describe
native set names, platform, parent/BIOS/disc dependencies and expected file
lengths/CRCs. No ROM, BIOS, decryption key or EEPROM payload is exported.
These are the emulator's own supported-set definitions, not a TrainerOS
gameplay-tested allowlist or a claim that every game supports two players.

License texts: LICENSE.upstream and LICENSE.arcade-metadata.
